WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:07.800
You touched my hand when I stretched them out so far...

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:18.860
Episode 2

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:18.860
First Star

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:21.610
Just one word is fine.

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:24.460
Just voice your dreams.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.580
It's your first step and first sign to realization.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.690
Ask yourself what is it that you like?

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.820
Your answers will...

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:39.800
blow your questions high into the sky.

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:36.230
Even more...

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.120
Like fireworks...

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:46.330
Even though we should all try to be more honest we ourselves, we can't.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:53.330
Maybe I should try summoning my soul as a child?

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:59.860
What touched my hand when i stretched them out so far...

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:05.010
was a Supernova that suddenly appear to this new night.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:10.970
For millions of light years, it never stops inside of me.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:19.190
The longer I gaze, the more power my eyes absorb...

00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:24.450
and that's because... because I'm a star too!

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:28.390
Akeno Mihoshi

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:30.920
Currently four people in the Astronomy Club:

00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:30.930
Ooyagi Saku

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:33.480
Yarai Sayo

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:35.900
Since there's less than five people, they're just a gathering of fanatics?!

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:35.890
Roma Takeyasu

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:39.090
The cherry blossom season has finally come to an end...

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:44.640
Yet the number of new Astronomy Club members still stands at zero.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:48.850
Why?!

00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:50.430
Nobody joined; there's nothing we can do about it.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:53.760
Though, I'm actually more interested to know why <i>you</i> are here today.

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:57.910
Especially when Saku-chan tried his best too!

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:57.640
I did not!

00:01:57.840 --> 00:01:59.400
I didn't try at all!

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.910
What are you talking about, Ooyagi?!

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:05.040
You're... You're with such beautiful seniors!

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:07.060
You're not being sincere enough!

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:08.730
Well, I don't consider Mihoshi one of them...

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:13.790
Well, everyone's trying their best, but the Student Council seems to have their eye on us.

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:16.890
The president is somewhat the cause too...

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:16.860
Hello, I'm from the Astronomy Club.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.750
There are times when his efforts tend to backfire.

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:20.230
You're really working hard.

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:20.230
Ghibli... Ghibli hair...

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:22.750
Edogawa-kun, you've signed up for the Photography Club, haven't you?

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:23.750
What a pity.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:26.200
What a pity.

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:27.360
What a pity.

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:29.560
Swimsuits...

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:32.900
Swimsuit photo shoots are calling to me!

00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:35.530
I'm sorry I couldn't live up to your expectations!

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:40.070
Look, look. That sophomore is here again.

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:42.020
Do you think they're going out?

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:43.640
What's so good about her?

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:46.990
Hime?

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:48.980
She's just an old lady.

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:51.520
Excuse me!

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:57.910
Why are you always hanging around a classroom full of freshmen?

00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:01.060
Sophomores should stick to their own classrooms!

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:02.920
H-H-Hime!

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:04.370
"Hime"?

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:05.440
Hime-chan?

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:07.800
Y-Yes, that's me.

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:11.690
I didn't know you were in this class!

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:11.960
What?

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:13.600
All the sophomore boys have been talking about you.

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:17.400
They were saying there was a cute freshman with fluffy hair!

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:19.330
I'm Akeno Mihoshi.

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:20.580
Nice to meet you, Hime-chan.

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:23.530
U-Um... I'm Makita Hime.

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:24.760
So? What is it?

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:26.720
Did you want to join the Astronomy Club?

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:28.210
Of course you can. Of course you can.

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:29.810
Just sign here.

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:30.160
What?!

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:31.590
That's not it!

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:33.440
Why are you here all the time?!

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:35.730
Fluffy~

00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:36.450
No!

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:39.800
Don't touch my hair!

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:41.670
Oh, the bell rang.

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:43.290
See you later!

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:45.540
Hey! Wait, Mihoshi!

00:03:48.190 --> 00:03:48.790
Makita-san.

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:54.140
Sorry for making you feel uncomfortable.

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:57.380
I keep telling Mihoshi not to visit, but...

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:00.250
It doesn't look like she'll listen.

00:03:58.410 --> 00:03:59.290
<i>He's using her first name...</i>

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:01.910
N-No, I'm fine.

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:03.690
You must have a hard time, Ooyagi-kun.

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:07.170
It's not like you're the one who's being a nuisance.

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:10.180
I guess they're going out after all...

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:12.840
Morning, everyone. Please sit down.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:14.220
Understood.

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:15.510
Thank you.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:19.000
You scared me.

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:20.540
You actually yelled at her.

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:22.800
Did Yarai-senpai say anything?

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:22.850
<i>Ooyagi-kun...</i>

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:23.390
Nope.

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:28.280
I first met Ooyagi-kun on the day of the entrance exam.

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:30.750
Please wait!

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:32.640
I wasn't accustomed to using public transportation...

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:36.060
Wet and messy, I became even more depressed.

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:40.090
I'm sorry-

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:45.140
I'm sorry!

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:45.800
I'm sorry!

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:47.990
I have a pair of scissors with me.

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:48.770
Let me just cut-

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:49.610
T-T-That hurts...

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:51.750
No, it's fine.

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:55.590
You've got beautiful hair, so...

00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:59.900
In that moment, I felt so much better.

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:01.440
There we go.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:04.130
T-Thank you very much.

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:07.300
They say my hair is fluffy now,

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:10.930
but I've always had a complex about it.

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:14.340
When I was little, it was curlier.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:15.350
It was totally out of control.

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:16.980
My nickname then was "Dwarf."

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:20.080
You've got beautiful hair, so...

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:25.330
And that's why I was so happy when he said it so casually.

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:31.970
And when I found out in the spring that we would be in the same class, I thought it had to be fate.

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:40.610
Yet he didn't remember who I was...

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:43.690
But! I won't lose!

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:46.250
I don't care if he's got an older girlfriend!

00:05:46.670 --> 00:05:48.270
I no longer have a hair complex!

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:51.460
Hey, don't tell me you're Dwarf?

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:52.810
I went to the same elementary school-

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:00.860
But ultimately, only classmates get to be with him all the time.

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:04.080
Ooyagi-kun, it's about the day duty.

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:06.430
Sensei said he wanted us to stay behind after class.

00:06:08.270 --> 00:06:09.770
They've multiplied!

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:13.830
Hime-chan, you have no idea how terrifying Fumin is.

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:18.410
We wanted to spend lunchtimes in our club room...

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:19.310
But...

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:20.820
But Fumin...

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:23.890
Paper: Days remaining before the Astronomy Club ceases to exist:

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:24.160
Three days left...

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:29.160
She's counting down the number of days left with her personal paper calendar right outside our club room!

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:33.440
She was even measuring the room in preparation for taking it over the other day!

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:34.800
I don't care!

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:38.290
Anyway, we freshmen need to get to know each other better!

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:39.900
So, you can all just leave!

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:41.380
I'm a freshman too.

00:06:41.970 --> 00:06:43.440
Now, now. Calm down.

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:45.730
Being so excitable is bad for your healt-

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:56.620
I'm surprised you joined that club, Ooyagi-kun.

00:06:57.980 --> 00:06:59.280
Well, I just somehow ended up joining...

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:03.030
I think there are other clubs that suit you a lot better.

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:04.010
For example, there's the basketball club,

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:05.420
or even the nihilistic cheer squad.

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:07.100
The Student Council's not a bad idea either.

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:07.180
Sorry?

00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:10.070
What club were you a member of when you were in middle school?

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:12.130
For the majority of it, I don't think I was in any clubs.

00:07:12.650 --> 00:07:15.250
I transfered schools so often I was never a member of any club for long.

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:19.800
Now that you mention it, you did say something about Fukuoka in your introductory speech.

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:20.670
Yup.

00:07:21.010 --> 00:07:24.380
Before that, I lived in Miyagi, Nara, and Osaka.

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:25.430
That many places?!

00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:28.300
And then my parents bought a house here, so I moved here.

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:30.310
That's amazing...

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:31.970
I've never experienced anything like that.

00:07:32.570 --> 00:07:36.010
I even chose to commute to a private middle school further away just so I could change my living environment.

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:39.400
T-There wasn't a particular reason behind that decision.

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:42.920
Huh? Then when did you meet Mihoshi-senpai?

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:49.160
Mihoshi... I lived in the area about seven years ago.

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:53.130
I hadn't seen her since I moved away in second grade,

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:54.750
but by sheer coincidence, I met her at this school.

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:57.160
Then things just kind of rolled along...

00:07:57.460 --> 00:07:58.120
Seven years...

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:00.980
I was rather surprised because she hasn't changed one bit.

00:08:01.650 --> 00:08:06.830
Also, this is the first time I've moved to a place where there's someone who knows me already...

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:08.200
someone who remembers me.

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:13.510
Makita-san?

00:08:14.330 --> 00:08:21.380
T-There might be more who remember you...

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:24.840
They may not know you from seven years ago or something like that,

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:28.740
but if you treasure the thought, it's still a memory, right?

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:30.970
Y-You know...

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:33.080
I-I...

00:08:33.290 --> 00:08:34.900
Saku-chan!

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:39.560
Mihoshi!

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:40.870
What happened to recruiting?

00:08:41.090 --> 00:08:42.750
That's what I've been doing up till now.

00:08:43.070 --> 00:08:43.710
Any luck?

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:45.390
Nope, none at all.

00:08:45.850 --> 00:08:49.140
But since it's a good opportunity, I thought we could stargaze on the rooftop.

00:08:49.390 --> 00:08:50.540
Saku-chan, you're coming too, right?

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:52.650
Then ask me like a normal person would! Normal!

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:55.290
How about you, Hime-chan?

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:56.770
It'll be fun.

00:08:57.030 --> 00:08:58.820
I...

00:08:58.990 --> 00:08:59.750
Oh, come on.

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:00.900
Hurry up.

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:11.530
Why do I...

00:09:16.810 --> 00:09:18.280
Look! It's the first star!

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:18.700
What?

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:25.650
The first star really does exist...

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:29.710
Although, there isn't actually a star called the First Star.

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:34.460
The first star is Venus because we can see it in the western sky at this time of the year.

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:37.460
Even though it's still bright outside...

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:39.280
The evening star.

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:40.740
Its apparent magnitude is minus four.

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:43.420
It's a hundred times brighter than stars of the first magnitude.

00:09:44.190 --> 00:09:45.790
Although, it's kind of hard to believe.

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:48.420
Saku-chan...

00:09:48.930 --> 00:09:52.310
That's because you were always talking about it, so I happened to remember it!

00:09:52.620 --> 00:09:54.160
You're being modest!

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:55.980
Oh, Saku-chan~

00:09:54.530 --> 00:09:55.740
Stop it!

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:56.720
Let go!

00:09:56.980 --> 00:09:58.920
You don't have to be embarrassed!

00:09:57.610 --> 00:09:59.450
<i>I guess I don't stand a chance with him...</i>

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:03.970
A beautiful first star.

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:06.750
The star that shines first.

00:10:08.030 --> 00:10:11.650
I can't possibly compete against her when they've been going out for seven years...

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:13.980
Those two aren't going out.

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:14.540
What?

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:17.000
Right, Yarai-kun?

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:17.880
Yes.

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:18.670
What?

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:21.680
Nope, we're not going out.

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:22.900
It's impossible!

00:10:26.110 --> 00:10:26.970
Mr. President.

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:27.730
Yes?

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:30.970
I'll join the Astronomy Club.

00:10:32.290 --> 00:10:33.110
Really?!

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:36.430
All right!

00:10:36.790 --> 00:10:38.780
I'm so happy-I'm dizzy...

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:39.690
President!

00:10:41.500 --> 00:10:45.240
The light of the stars will eventually reach you even if it isn't the first to shine.

00:10:46.230 --> 00:10:48.390
What's most important is the future.

00:10:54.530 --> 00:10:59.050
Well then, to celebrate our future...

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:01.220
Cheers!

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:02.230
Thank goodness.

00:11:02.620 --> 00:11:04.560
Edogawa, don't you belong in the Photography Club?

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:06.850
Come on now, don't be so picky.

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:08.790
Now, Saku-chan, drink up, drink up!

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:11.940
We can finally ease off on the recruiting and start our activities.

00:11:12.080 --> 00:11:16.160
Ooyagi-kun, let's be friends - both here and as classmates.

00:11:17.910 --> 00:11:23.000
Oh my, old lady, are you planning to interfere between two new members trying to get to know one another?

00:11:23.380 --> 00:11:28.000
New members should stick together with other new members.

00:11:34.510 --> 00:11:36.360
Hime-chan, you're so cute.

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:37.290
No!

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:39.560
Where did my quiet high school life disappear to?

00:11:40.020 --> 00:11:41.920
But I hear it was a complete mess.

00:11:42.280 --> 00:11:44.210
President Kotodzuka was furious.

00:11:44.730 --> 00:11:46.340
Haraguchi-kun looked lifeless.

00:11:46.340 --> 00:11:47.430
I feel sorry for him.

00:11:47.820 --> 00:11:49.770
She really hates us, doesn't she?

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:51.180
For personal reasons.

00:11:51.750 --> 00:11:53.230
Don't worry. Don't worry.

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:56.220
She won't complain as long as we function properly.

00:11:56.980 --> 00:11:58.840
Anyway, let's forget about everything except drinking today!

00:11:58.890 --> 00:12:00.870
Now, now, let's drink up...

00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:03.410
Fumin!

00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:05.510
As expected from a useless club.

00:12:05.810 --> 00:12:07.200
Having a toast in your club room?

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:08.370
How wonderful.

00:12:08.430 --> 00:12:10.360
N-No alcohol!

00:12:10.060 --> 00:12:10.720
That's obvious!

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:11.300
L-Lifeless...

00:12:11.400 --> 00:12:14.530
I've looked through the plans you submitted...

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:18.170
But can this even be called a plan?

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:21.200
I'll try to understand the aim of your club,

00:12:21.380 --> 00:12:24.060
but I'd like you to learn more from other clubs too.

00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:28.010
As a side note, the Literature Club takes place whatever the weather.

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:29.890
Let's go, Haraguchi.

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:37.180
But you know, she does have a point.

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:41.870
I'm sure there are a lot of people who don't know what we do.

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:46.110
I think our club should function by trying to appeal to others more.

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:49.770
Therefore, tonight, we'll hold a stargazing session.

00:12:50.750 --> 00:12:52.020
T-That's rather sudden, isn't it?

00:12:52.060 --> 00:12:53.360
Are you sure it's going to be okay?

00:12:53.480 --> 00:12:54.340
Don't worry.

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:56.730
It's the perfect opportunity for us to get to know each other too.

00:12:56.370 --> 00:12:57.720
All right!

00:12:57.290 --> 00:13:00.650
More importantly, I sense that the weather will be good tonight!

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:06.120
The weather's terrible!

00:13:06.810 --> 00:13:08.250
It was raining the other day too.

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:11.540
Could one of us be cursed with bad weather?

00:13:11.540 --> 00:13:14.060
Stop saying that and try to stay dry.

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:16.030
Oh no! My hair!

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:17.820
This is a Wisteria trellis!

00:13:19.030 --> 00:13:20.220
What should we do?

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:22.700
For the time being, we need to take cover from the rain.

00:13:23.020 --> 00:13:24.070
True...

00:13:24.460 --> 00:13:25.750
Oh, really?

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:27.960
Yes, I'm really happy.

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:29.360
Yes. Yes.

00:13:29.810 --> 00:13:30.140
Okay.

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:31.020
See you in a bit.

00:13:33.260 --> 00:13:36.000
I got permission to visit Saku-chan's house!

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:37.060
What?

00:13:37.060 --> 00:13:38.620
H-How do you know my number?!

00:13:38.770 --> 00:13:39.990
The members list.

00:13:40.720 --> 00:13:43.140
Let's go and visit despite knowing that we'll be an inconvenience.

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:45.470
We'll just get wet if we stay here.

00:13:45.540 --> 00:13:46.320
Yay!

00:13:46.320 --> 00:13:47.280
It's too sudden!

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:48.820
I'm sure you all have other plans!

00:13:49.110 --> 00:13:50.540
Besides, even if you come to my house-

00:13:50.750 --> 00:13:52.400
We really want to go!

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:56.140
Sorry!

00:13:57.360 --> 00:13:58.820
This is my house.

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:02.270
Ooyagi-kun's house...

00:14:03.870 --> 00:14:04.580
I'm home-

00:14:06.100 --> 00:14:08.020
Welcome, Mii-chan!

00:14:08.390 --> 00:14:10.160
It must've been hard on you to be in the rain.

00:14:10.270 --> 00:14:11.480
Oh my, and who might you be?

00:14:11.610 --> 00:14:12.720
Are you friends from his club?

00:14:12.840 --> 00:14:14.740
Oh my, they're all beautiful girls!

00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:16.260
Aren't you lucky, Saku.

00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:19.170
She... She resembles someone we know...

00:14:16.520 --> 00:14:17.730
Now, now. Come in.

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:22.950
Oh my, you're all grown up now.

00:14:23.360 --> 00:14:24.850
I've always wanted to see you again.

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:27.620
Did that injury leave any scars?

00:14:27.830 --> 00:14:30.030
Nope, I'm perfectly fine!

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:33.040
I'm sorry. Saku's such a weakling.

00:14:33.070 --> 00:14:33.980
Shut up!

00:14:36.610 --> 00:14:38.150
We want to see your room.

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:39.110
Absolutely not!

00:14:39.350 --> 00:14:40.290
Especially not you, Mihoshi!

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:42.720
Saku-chan~!

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:45.020
I said no, no, no!

00:14:48.390 --> 00:14:50.520
What if they end up staying here?!

00:14:53.290 --> 00:14:54.790
But you know, I'm so happy.

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:57.740
It's been a while since Saku brought friends home.

00:14:58.510 --> 00:15:01.420
He's had to transfer schools so many times; I'm sure he's had a hard time.

00:15:01.720 --> 00:15:06.060
Excuse me, but what was he like at his previous school?

00:15:06.690 --> 00:15:08.480
Let's see...

00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:10.070
He read a lot of books;

00:15:10.370 --> 00:15:12.360
although, he still does that now.

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:17.180
But he was most animated living here,

00:15:17.730 --> 00:15:20.640
which is why I've always wanted to come back here.

00:15:21.050 --> 00:15:23.530
Plus living here means he'll be able to attend universities in Tokyo in the future.

00:15:23.950 --> 00:15:27.760
But I made him transfer schools again, so it's really just my selfishness.

00:15:28.230 --> 00:15:31.040
But I'm glad we came back.

00:15:31.980 --> 00:15:32.660
Mom...

00:15:33.380 --> 00:15:36.640
Oh yeah, he smiles a lot these days.

00:15:37.060 --> 00:15:39.890
He tries to act all cool, but actually, his face gives it away.

00:15:40.090 --> 00:15:42.260
Hey! Stop telling them things that could ruin my image!

00:15:42.930 --> 00:15:44.420
Okay, it's ready.

00:15:44.800 --> 00:15:46.720
Everyone, don't be modest and eat lots, okay?

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:47.900
Ooyagi!

00:15:47.980 --> 00:15:48.540
Let's be friends.

00:15:48.760 --> 00:15:50.130
Let's be good friends!

00:15:50.240 --> 00:15:52.660
Call me your best friend!

00:15:52.770 --> 00:15:53.650
Okay, okay...

00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:54.790
What the hell is that?

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:56.650
Open up to me more!

00:15:56.990 --> 00:15:58.230
I'm sorry we dropped by without warning.

00:15:58.370 --> 00:15:59.650
Thank you for the food.

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:00.610
Sure.

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:01.810
Come again.

00:16:02.620 --> 00:16:03.760
I'll walk you guys to the bus stop.

00:16:04.070 --> 00:16:04.850
It's fine.

00:16:05.320 --> 00:16:06.540
I'll see you tomorrow at school!

00:16:06.760 --> 00:16:08.000
Bye, Saku-chan!

00:16:08.210 --> 00:16:09.610
And thanks, Saku's Mom!

00:16:10.120 --> 00:16:11.210
Mii-chan.

00:16:11.910 --> 00:16:14.110
Tell your mother and father that I said, "Hi."

00:16:17.690 --> 00:16:18.280
I will!

00:16:19.490 --> 00:16:21.880
Saku-chan, come and visit me anytime, okay?

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:21.900
Bye.

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:31.610
And thus, we gave stargazing another attempt the next day...

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:33.560
Perfect.

00:16:37.590 --> 00:16:40.310
Today, I get to see him at night, not in a school uniform.

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:44.300
What's more, we might even get to ride his bike!

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:44.090
Sign: Prince Charming's Bike

00:16:44.330 --> 00:16:46.340
Hime, hang on tight.

00:16:46.390 --> 00:16:48.020
What if!

00:16:48.060 --> 00:16:50.020
I'm so glad I joined the Astronomy Club!

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:52.250
Ooyagi-kun!

00:16:53.960 --> 00:16:55.920
No, Hime-chan!

00:16:57.610 --> 00:17:00.850
If you're dressed like that, you never know when they'll attack!

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:01.790
A-Attack?!

00:17:01.920 --> 00:17:03.130
Mosquitoes!

00:17:03.620 --> 00:17:06.510
I'm glad I came prepared for this though.

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:07.720
Now, change into this.

00:17:07.810 --> 00:17:09.290
R-Right here?!

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:10.020
No...

00:17:10.020 --> 00:17:12.000
No!

00:17:17.950 --> 00:17:19.480
Okay, let's go!

00:17:20.010 --> 00:17:22.560
T-This goes against my fashion sense!

00:17:23.360 --> 00:17:25.560
Now, Makita-kun, hop on.

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:25.920
What?

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:27.660
W-Why?

00:17:28.720 --> 00:17:33.180
[Note: MTB stands for Mountain Bike.]

00:17:30.920 --> 00:17:33.100
With high heels like yours, you'll need to sit.

00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:36.330
It's got a cushion too.

00:17:36.930 --> 00:17:38.910
President, do you want me to change places with you?

00:17:39.160 --> 00:17:40.130
Don't worry.

00:17:39.900 --> 00:17:43.360
Sign: The President - a man-on-a-mission

00:17:41.050 --> 00:17:43.420
Look. It's electrical.

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:46.420
It's a little far, but let's all try our best.

00:17:44.350 --> 00:17:45.000
<i>No...</i>

00:17:46.510 --> 00:17:46.970
No...

00:17:47.760 --> 00:17:48.390
No...

00:17:48.390 --> 00:17:53.160
No! No!

00:17:53.360 --> 00:17:54.890
P-President! Makita-san!

00:17:55.020 --> 00:17:57.220
No!

00:17:56.790 --> 00:17:58.930
No! Get a hold of yourself, President!

00:18:00.060 --> 00:18:01.870
Ah, it's the stars...

00:18:01.960 --> 00:18:02.850
It's the stars...

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:04.640
Can everyone else see them too?

00:18:04.640 --> 00:18:06.880
No!

00:18:11.210 --> 00:18:14.250
Somehow, I'm already dead tired...

00:18:14.610 --> 00:18:17.040
Let's allow those two to get a short break.

00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:18.620
Hang in there, President!

00:18:19.520 --> 00:18:22.410
The president had his reasons for coming here.

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:26.390
He probably wanted to show everyone the stars in the best possible environment.

00:18:28.740 --> 00:18:33.870
It's often misty in the spring and there aren't as many constellations as in the winter,

00:18:33.870 --> 00:18:35.080
so it gives the impression that they're really faint.

00:18:35.520 --> 00:18:37.910
But when it's clear, it's really beautiful.

00:18:38.880 --> 00:18:40.790
On a side note, the Big Dipper's at its best there.

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:42.310
I know that one!

00:18:42.340 --> 00:18:45.300
[Note: He's pretending to be Kenshiro from the series, Fist of the North Star.]

00:18:43.710 --> 00:18:45.360
Okay, enough. That's dangerous.

00:18:46.150 --> 00:18:47.280
The Shichousei, it's-

00:18:47.860 --> 00:18:49.110
Don't do that, Saku-chan.

00:18:49.260 --> 00:18:50.320
You need to allow your eyes to become accustomed to the dark.

00:18:50.640 --> 00:18:54.080
We came all this way into the darkness especially to avoid the moon and street lights.

00:18:54.450 --> 00:18:57.720
If you keep your light on, your eyes won't get accustomed to the dark.

00:18:58.320 --> 00:18:58.590
Here.

00:18:59.720 --> 00:19:02.150
It's better to put red cellophane paper over it,

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:05.660
but even just wrapping a red cloth around it makes it easier on the eyes.

00:19:06.320 --> 00:19:08.990
It's the exact same reason why red tail lamps on cars are easy on the eyes.

00:19:09.610 --> 00:19:10.550
I see.

00:19:12.600 --> 00:19:15.400
Look! The Big Dipper is high up in the northern sky,

00:19:15.960 --> 00:19:20.870
and if you extend the curve, it's Arcturus, also known as the Mugiboshi, the red star from the Boötes constellation.

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:24.230
Then, if you extend the curve even more, you reach the star Spica which forms part of the Virgo constellation.

00:19:24.860 --> 00:19:26.340
A pale white Shinjuboshi.

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:30.080
And what connects them all together is the Spring Curve.

00:19:31.960 --> 00:19:36.830
I like the Spring Triangle and the Spring Diamond too, but my favorite is the Curve.

00:19:37.280 --> 00:19:38.550
It looks just like a rocking chair.

00:19:38.650 --> 00:19:40.050
It makes me want to sit on it.

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:42.130
No, I think that depends on the person...

00:19:42.730 --> 00:19:47.440
Wow, it's a lot larger than I imagined from reading books.

00:19:47.920 --> 00:19:50.620
I always thought that constellations were more closely arranged together.

00:19:51.530 --> 00:19:52.950
[Note: Shichousei is a star that appeared in the series Fist of the Northern Star. Shichousei is the star Alcor next to Mizar.]

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:52.940
Do you want to see the Shichousei?

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:54.970
Or perhaps the nebula?

00:19:54.970 --> 00:19:55.530
Yes!

00:19:55.530 --> 00:19:56.180
I do! I do!

00:19:56.190 --> 00:19:56.810
I do!

00:19:57.290 --> 00:19:59.990
Astronomy Club Gadget, set on!

00:20:01.540 --> 00:20:02.470
Amazing.

00:20:03.180 --> 00:20:04.610
M-May I touch it?

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:05.520
Go ahead.

00:20:14.740 --> 00:20:15.430
Are you all right?

00:20:16.030 --> 00:20:16.600
Are you tired?

00:20:17.310 --> 00:20:18.670
S-Sayo-senpai.

00:20:19.090 --> 00:20:20.320
No, it's nothing.

00:20:21.170 --> 00:20:25.490
It just feels a little strange to be doing this at night.

00:20:26.590 --> 00:20:28.640
If you think about it, we're usually inside that light over there.

00:20:30.100 --> 00:20:34.600
Night falls upon everyone, but there are many ways to spend it.

00:20:36.340 --> 00:20:37.830
I'm saying something obvious, aren't I?

00:20:38.620 --> 00:20:39.080
Nope.

00:20:39.920 --> 00:20:40.940
I think so too.

00:20:41.740 --> 00:20:43.670
If I hadn't come back to this city,

00:20:44.320 --> 00:20:47.830
I'd probably be reading a book in some other city tonight too.

00:20:50.070 --> 00:20:55.600
I would never have thought about the small lights twinkling high above my roof as I read.

00:20:56.650 --> 00:20:57.630
Silence.

00:20:57.950 --> 00:20:59.180
Darkness.

00:20:59.470 --> 00:21:01.110
I know a lot of words,

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:05.920
but most of the nights I know were spent under an artificial light.

00:21:07.560 --> 00:21:08.840
I'm a little relieved.

00:21:10.360 --> 00:21:15.330
I was worried that you were still burdening yourself with what happened in elementary school.

00:21:15.890 --> 00:21:16.520
It doesn't matter.

00:21:17.180 --> 00:21:18.690
It's already in the past.

00:21:19.340 --> 00:21:21.220
If it were now, I can...

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:24.400
Ow!

00:21:24.790 --> 00:21:26.310
Take care of Mihoshi, okay?

00:21:26.570 --> 00:21:27.220
What?

00:21:27.980 --> 00:21:30.680
Saku-chan! Sayo-chin!

00:21:30.940 --> 00:21:31.900
What are you doing?

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:33.440
Hurry up and come over here!

00:21:33.470 --> 00:21:35.150
Ooyagi, what should I do?

00:21:35.150 --> 00:21:37.070
I think I'm hooked!

00:21:37.370 --> 00:21:42.750
[Note: Ultraman comes from the M-78 Nebula.]

00:21:37.380 --> 00:21:42.750
The M from M-78 Nebula wasn't just from Ultraman!

00:21:42.870 --> 00:21:44.600
Edogawa-kun, you're so smart!

00:21:45.790 --> 00:21:46.720
I'm hooked!

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:49.070
I'm hooked!

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:51.960
The star's light and the city's light...

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:54.900
Neither is right nor wrong.

00:21:58.620 --> 00:22:01.300
But nights like this aren't bad either.

00:22:07.460 --> 00:22:07.820
But...

00:22:09.110 --> 00:22:11.260
Not this!

00:22:11.880 --> 00:22:14.860
I won't lose no matter what!

00:22:22.380 --> 00:22:26.730
I look up at the sky, and I think of you…

00:22:27.030 --> 00:22:30.410
but I can’t find the words,

00:22:31.550 --> 00:22:33.710
I want to tell you,

00:22:33.710 --> 00:22:36.230
but they just slip away…

00:22:36.530 --> 00:22:39.900
almost like Shooting Stars.

00:22:40.390 --> 00:22:44.480
In this Wave of Silence,

00:22:44.860 --> 00:22:48.850
a ray of light flickers the darkness

00:22:49.320 --> 00:22:54.160
playing with my memories

00:22:54.160 --> 00:23:00.000
and releasing my heart.

00:23:00.830 --> 00:23:02.940
Into the future,

00:23:02.940 --> 00:23:11.510
I will have these feelings again!

00:23:11.920 --> 00:23:15.920
No worries, I’m not alone.

00:23:16.170 --> 00:23:21.010
You have taught me I’m not alone.

00:23:21.010 --> 00:23:29.920
Listen to my “Twinkle” story!

00:23:30.070 --> 00:23:34.100
Maybe my voice would reach you.

00:23:35.470 --> 00:23:40.350
I look up at the sky, surrounded by Stardust!

00:23:44.760 --> 00:23:49.770
Sora no Manimani

00:23:44.760 --> 00:23:49.770
Next time: Planetarium

00:23:45.400 --> 00:23:46.970
Next time, on Sora no Manimani:

00:23:47.370 --> 00:23:48.160
Planetarium.

00:23:48.530 --> 00:23:49.660
I won't let you sleep tonight.

00:23:49.770 --> 00:23:54.770
In the continuous rainy weather,

00:23:49.770 --> 00:23:54.770
Mihoshi's Life Points are at zero!!

00:23:54.770 --> 00:23:59.780
At such a time, everyone

00:23:54.770 --> 00:23:59.780
gets a complementary tour of the stars!!
